15
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:39,480
I'm a failure.

16
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:40,680
I'm a failure.

17
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,000
I'm a failure.

18
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,800
Sir.

19
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,800
My mom...

20
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,280
My mom never had a single day of happiness.

21
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:52,440
She never had a single good day.

22
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,720
Mr. Chen

23
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,920
Take a look. Is this it?

24
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:43,960
Thank you.

25
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,480
Thank you.

26
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,080
I'm sorry for your loss.

27
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:01,400
Mom

28
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,080
Mom

29
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:07,800
Mom

30
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,640
How did you find it?

31
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,560
I guessed.

32
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:25,800
Mom

33
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:36,640
You know,

34
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:40,920
living in this city has actually been pretty nice all these years.

35
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:41,760
Yeah, it has.

36
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:44,920
So I wanted to take a good look before I leave.

37
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:48,560
Sometimes it feels like so much has changed.

38
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:50,840
But also like nothing has changed at all.

39
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:56,240
From up here,

40
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:58,920
our city looks so big.

41
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,800
Because you've never left it.

42
