66
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,200
Why?

67
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:33,600
If it weren't for your superpower,

68
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,720
they probably wouldn't have found his bracelet.

69
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:40,600
That's true.

70
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,000
Isn't there a saying?

71
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:46,280
Prejudice in people's minds is like a massive mountain.

72
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,160
So when we

73
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:50,880
stand at the bottom, we can only see its surface.

74
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:54,040
Actually, I was a bit prejudiced today too.

75
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:56,360
I thought he was just a greedy, ungrateful son.

76
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:03,240
Do you know why I don't want to do this job?

77
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:06,440
Ever since I was little,

78
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:09,760
I've seen people tear each other apart at funerals.

79
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:12,640
And I've seen so many life-and-death partings.

80
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:14,560
I've always felt this job is very...

81
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,760
tragic and soul-crushing.

82
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,120
Well, I'm quite different from you.

83
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,360
At first, I felt that

84
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:26,280
being able to experience the deceased's past

85
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,400
and their feelings

86
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,280
was like a curse.

87
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,440
But now I feel that

88
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:33,240
this superpower

89
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,560
is actually more like a blessed gift.

90
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:37,520
What?

91
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:39,040
Superpower?

92
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:40,720
Yiran.

93
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,240
You have superpowers?

94
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:53,600
Psychometry.

95
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,600
Whenever I touch the belongings of the deceased,

96
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:04,280
certain sounds, images,

97
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,320
and even smells

98
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,920
will flood into my mind.

99
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:08,840
I can even feel

100
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:11,440
the deceased's joys and sorrows.

101
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:12,760
I can vouch for that.

102
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:16,920
A Min,

103
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:18,160
you've lived a long time.

104
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:19,320
Analyze this for us.

105
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,960
Can you figure anything out?

106
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,560
Before your mother passed away,

107
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,640
she said she wanted some oranges.

108
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,440
You went out and brought some back,

109
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:21,440
but before she could eat them,

110
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:22,400
she...

111
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,600
Exactly.

112
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,440
Actually, I've done a lot of research,

113
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:56,840
but couldn't find a perfect explanation.

114
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:00,240
There's Zhuangzi's Butterfly Dream,

115
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:04,600
and Alice in Wonderland Syndrome.

116
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,040
Psychometry.

117
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,560
It sounds pretty mystical,

118
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:13,000
but the world is vast and full of wonders.

119
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:13,800
Our understanding

120
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:15,280
is just the tip of the iceberg.

121
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,400
In this world,

122
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,840
there are indeed some people

123
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:20,320
whose synesthesia is beyond the ordinary.

124
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,840
For example, Da Vinci,

125
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,720
David Hockney...

126
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,960
These famous artists,

127
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:28,360
their talents might just stem from this.

128
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:32,280
So you're saying

129
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:35,240
Yiran essentially possesses a key

130
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:37,720
that can unlock the door to the past.

131
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:39,440
You could also say

132
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,880
Yiran is The Chosen Funeral Director.

133
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:46,840
For the deceased,

134
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,400
there's always something they want to leave behind

135
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,080
as a memento for the living.

136
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,080
Because a person truly dies

137
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:57,080
when they are forgotten by the living.

138
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,800
If you can make good use of this gift,

139
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,760
